<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fourteen sub-Saharan colonies and trust territories become independent</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/venezuela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Venezuela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Venezuela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Venezuela co-founds OPEC at Baghdad</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Belgium.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Belgium</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Belgian Congo becomes independent</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Nepal.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Nepal</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King Mahendra dismisses parliament and introduces the panchayat system</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/union-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Union%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Union of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Police kill 69 protesters at Sharpeville; white voters approve a republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Somaliland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Somaliland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British Somaliland is independent for five days, then unites with Somalia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Police kill 69 protesters at Sharpeville, and the ANC and the PAC are banned</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/colonial-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Colonial%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Colonial rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The UN General Assembly declares the right of colonial peoples to independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/ubaid-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ubaid%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ubaid culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Joan Oates shows that the Eridu and Hajji Muhammed styles belong to the Ubaid and divides it into phases</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/negritude"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/N%C3%A9gritude.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Négritude</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Wole Soyinka mocks Négritude’s “duikeritude”, and Paulette Nardal complains of the neglect of her and her sister’s part</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lê Duẩn's leadership begins, and the North goes to war with the Republic of Vietnam through its proxy the Viet Cong</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/kwame-nkrumah"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kwame%20Nkrumah.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kwame Nkrumah</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ghana becomes a republic and Nkrumah is elected its president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/guru-granth-sahib"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Guru%20Granth%20Sahib.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Guru Granth Sahib</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gopal Singh publishes the first complete English translation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mumbai"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mumbai.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mumbai</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Bombay becomes the capital of the new state of Maharashtra</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/rio-de-janeiro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rio%20de%20Janeiro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rio de Janeiro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital of Brazil moves from Rio to Brasília</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/arthashastra"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Arthashastra.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Arthashastra</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">R. P. Kangle publishes a critical edition based on all the available manuscripts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/patrice-lumumba"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Patrice%20Lumumba.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Patrice Lumumba</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence is declared on 30 June; Lumumba, prime minister since the vote of 23 and 24 June, gives his impromptu speech, and the army mutiny of July opens the Congo Crisis</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/patrice-lumumba"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Patrice%20Lumumba.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Patrice Lumumba</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kasa-Vubu dismisses him on 5 September; Mobutu announces a coup on 14 September; Mobutu's troops arrest Lumumba at the Sankuru River on 1 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The First Lancaster House Conference sets native Kenyan majority rule in motion</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Senegal becomes independent and Léopold Senghor is elected its president</span></li></ul></section>
